{
  "dom_id": "step-648009",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Finding a Value Given a Ratio by Rounding an Amount",
  "problem": "The ratio of the number of orchids to the number of roses in a garden is $1: 3.$ In the garden, there are $84$ orchids. Rounding the number of orchids to the nearest ten, approximate the number of roses in the garden.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the number of orchids:\n\n$$\n84 \\longrightarrow 80\n$$\n\nWe are told that ratio of the number of orchids to the number of roses in the garden is $1:3,$ which can be expressed as the fraction\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\color{red}3} \\, .\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents the number of orchids and the denominator represents the number of roses.\n\nWe know that there are approximately $80$ orchids, so we want to make a numerator of $80.$ We can do this by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $80\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1 \\times 80}{3 \\times 80} = \\dfrac{80}{240}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $240$ roses in the garden.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
